and effective detector based on ML and fingerprinting has been considered and implemented to evaluate its performance while detecting the proposed attacks. More in detail, natural language processing (NLP) techniques have been employed by the detector to process the system call traces into numerical values. After that, unsupervised ML algorithms based on anomaly detection have been used to predict normal and malicious behaviors. According to the obtained results, it can be concluded that existing detection systems are not reliable in identifying the new SSDF attacks. This is because the new implementation requires fewer system calls to access kernel space and consequently produces fewer detectable anomalies.

As future work, it is planned to work on detection systems that consider novel data sources able to model the small perturbations added by the new SSDF attacks implemented in the sensor memory. It is also planned to evaluate the SSDF attacks and detection systems in several spectrum sensors with different hardware and software configurations.

